            <div>
                <p>
                    <hi rend="figure">STALKED</hi>
                </p>
                
                <div>
                    <p>
                        If you're going to San Francsico...
                        We are losing people to the south. On 
                        their way are Annie, Tammy Smith, 
                        Jerri, and the Little Magnets (Paul Hood, 
                        Dame Dimitri, Lee Lumsden). Farewell...
                    </p>
                    
                    <p>
                        Is it true Time Travelers is looking to 
                        open a club/theater in Pioneer Square?? 
                        Cellophane Square will be producing a 
                        show May 25th at Washington Hall......
                        Featuring The Cheaters and The Radios.
                    </p>
                    
                    <p>
                        Suprise band gigging in Seattle lately: 
                        The Fishsticks. Who says bubblegum rock 
                        is dead??
                    </p>
                    
                    <p>
                        Expect an extravaganza! The Dead Kennedy's 
                        will be here <date>July 13 &amp; 14</date>. Brought to 
                        you by Time Travelers
                    </p>
                    
                    <p>
                        The first new wave band to come out from 
                        the wilds of Bellingham is called The 
                        Accident.
                    </p>
                </div>
                    
                    <div>
                        <figure></figure>
                    </div>
                    
                 <div>
                     <p>
                         News from the Readymades.....
                         They are only two to three weeks away 
                         from a recording contract, says bassist 
                         Wayne Deitzel. The band has some gigs 
                         lined up, including opening for Tom 
                         Robinson, and playing second bill to Roxy 
                         Music. The band is still working with 
                         Sandy Pearlman, and may be signed by one 
                         of the following labels: Warner Bros., 
                         Electra, Mercury, and get this: RSO. 
                         Watch out Bee Gees!!
                     </p>
                 </div>
                
                    <div>
                        <p>
                            -- -- -- --
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    
                 <div>
                     <p>
                         If you dont already know, The Mentors 
                         are dead. Rumor has it that Eldon is in 
                         LA to form a new band. Son of Mentor????
                     </p>
                 </div>
                    
                    <div>
                        <p>
                            -- -- -- --
                        </p>
                    </div>
                
                </div>
                
                <div>
                    <p>STELAZINE</p>
                    <p>THORAZINE</p>
                    
                    <p>
                        One of the "mind drugs" much perscribed.
                        Adverse side effects are not uncommonly enco-
                        untered with all phenothiasines, which should 
                        therefore be reserved for situations serious 
                        enough to warrant thier use (usually, frank 
                        prychosis). It is among the 100 top drugs..
                    </p>        
                </div>
                
                <div>
                    <p>
                        Rock against Racism chapters are forming 
                        around the USA. Concerts are being planed. 
                        If youre interested, contact them 
                        in Ny at: 
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                PO Box 392, Canal St. Sta. NYC 
                                10013
                            </addrLine>
                        </address> 
                        (212) 553-5028
                        The Cheaters have a new drummer: James 
                            Gascoigne.........
                    </p>
                </div>
                    
                    <div>
                        <figure></figure>
                    </div>
                    
                 <div>
                    <p>
                        Vinyl out from Ian Fisher soon. A-side 
                        has an ex-Telepath back up, and B-side 
                        has an ex-Invader backup. Noy bad.....
                    </p>
                    
                    <p>
                        The Moderley's continue to gig around 
                        town, getting a great share of local 
                        newspaper publicity. So how come most 
                        people don't like them. Do Patrick and 
                        George known something the rest of us 
                        don't?? Maybe it's all in knowing the 
                        right people....
                    </p>
                    
                    <p>
                        Ex-Generator (and ex-e member) Mitchael 
                            Wonderful is the new Enemy bass player..
                        George returns to rhythm.
                    </p>
                    
                    <p>
                        Be on the lookout for a great new single 
                        for Ice 9. Featured are: "Out, Out, Out", 
                        "Revolting Mess", and "27.3". It's gonna 
                        be great!!
                    </p>
                    
                    <p>
                        The next show: May 19 8PM at Washington 
                        Hall (14th and Fir), featuring: The Dils 
                        DOA and Chinas Comidas. A Robert Benne-
                        tt/Wes (second Time Round) Production.
                    </p>
                    
                    <p>
                        Greg Scars has left the Avengers to form 
                        a new band. His replacement is Brad Kunt 
                        (ex-DOA).
                    </p> 
                    
                    <p>
                        Are Time Travelers bringing the Screamers 
                        to Seattle? Is Roger Husbands? Who 
                        will win?
                    </p>
                 </div>
            
                    <div>
                        <figure></figure>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div>
                        <p>
                            Gina and Gary (ex-Generator) were recen-
                            tly married in a Canadian extravaganza..
                            We at STELLAZINE send them a mint copy of 
                            "Gimme Money"......
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            Look for the new Offs single on Walking 
                            Dead Productions. "Jonny Too Bad" b/w 
                            "624803". Soon back from a stint in NY.
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            New Avengers single produced by ex-Pistol 
                            Steve Jones includes "White ******". Are 
                            they on their way to an English record 
                            company contract?????
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            And finally, Seattle will be back on the 
                            concert path in about a month. The cir-
                            cuit will be Portland, Seattle and Vanc-
                            ouver....We can't wait!!!!
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            The X-Men have disbanded. Gregor and 
                            Glen are writing music together.
                            Dickle fever will engulf Seattle in a 
                            couple of months when they return from 
                            a European tour.....
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            Engineer Harry Cool has formed a record 
                            label for the area. First band to sign: 
                            Ice 9. Look for possible vinyl fom some 
                            Seattle bands...... The name? Vynyl Re-
                            cords......
                        </p>
                    </div>
            
                    <div>
                        <figure></figure>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div>
                        <p>
                            Ex-Clones Jeff and Sheldon are in SF to 
                            form a new band.
                        </p> 
                        
                        <p>
                            Radio news: Kim has not been kicked out. 
                            Allan will do vocals, and a new guitar-
                            ist has been added. Look for a possible 
                            gig in May with the Cheaters, produced 
                            by Cellophane Square.....
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            Randy Pandora (ex-Generator) has a new 
                            band: The Detectives
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            New on the concert promotion scene: Time 
                            Travelers and Cellophane Square.
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            The News: Rick Ricks
                            <lb/>Kelly N. K.
                            <lb/>Tommy Sero
                            <lb/>Roz Darrell
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            Rock Against Sexism:
                            <address>
                                <addrLine>e/o 121 Grandison Road</addrLine>
                                <addrLine>London S.W.11 England</addrLine>
                            </address>
                        </p>
                        
                        <p>
                            Two New bands to look for:
                            The Innocents (with Jeff Larson)
                            and,
                            The Blackouts: Bill Reiflin
                            <lb/>Roland
                            <lb/>Mike Davidson
                            <lb/>Eric Werner
                        </p>
                        
